  "result": "Perfect! All 104 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**src/invoices.js** \u2014 Added VAT calculation:\n\n**`lineVat(line)`** \u2014 Calculates VAT on a line's amount after discount:\n- Amount = lineTotal - lineDiscount\n- VAT = (amount \u00d7 vatRate / 100), rounded per line\n\n**`invoiceTotals(invoice)`** \u2014 Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`:\n- `subtotal` = sum of undiscounted line totals\n- `discount` = sum of line discounts\n- `vat` = sum of rounded line VATs (calculated on discounted amounts)\n- `total` = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n\n**src/render.js** \u2014 Updated to display VAT:\n- Shows VAT on each line when discount is present (after the discount)\n- Displays `Subtotal:` when VAT is present (even without discount)\n- Shows `VAT:` line before the final `Total:` when VAT > 0\n- Formats all amounts with `formatEuros()`\n\n**Key design decision:** VAT is calculated per line on the discounted amount, then rounded per line. The invoice VAT is the sum of these rounded line VATs, never a percentage of the invoice total.\n\n**Tests** \u2014 Added 14 comprehensive tests:\n- 8 for invoices module: VAT on undiscounted/discounted lines, different rates (0/9/21%), VAT in totals\n- 6 for render: VAT display with/without discounts, 0% VAT products, VAT placement above total\n\nAll 104 tests pass \u2713",
